Lua 5.5.1 (https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.5.1.tar.gz,
sha256 1c4b4068d67061f2a2231ad2b5422e77acea1487ea9890f6320af614f4373dce),
src/ only: the core, lauxlib and the base, coroutine, string, table, math and
utf8 libraries. Not included: lua.c, luac.c, linit.c and the io, os, package
(loadlib) and debug libraries. Changes, all marked "Solana OS":
- luaconf.h: LUA_32BITS on, LUAI_MAXCCALLS 64, MAXCCALLS 32;
  luai_cstackfull() hooks the host's native C stack guard, which ldo.c
  (ccall) and lstate.c (luaE_incCstack, luaE_checkcstack) also check;
  luai_userstatethread arms the count hook on new coroutines;
  LUA_SOLANA_LUAC labels this build's binary chunks (the store's compiler,
  tools/luac, is built from these sources).
- lstrlib.c charges pattern matching and plain find work to the host's
  instruction budget (luai_patternsteps), and leaves string.dump out.
- lapi.c adds lua_pushfilled (declared in lua.h), a string filled in place,
  so file reads need no second buffer.
- lauxlib.c/.h: luaL_newlib makes lazy libraries (luaL_newlazylib): an empty
  table whose functions come from the library's static luaL_Reg array on
  first use, so the arrays stay in flash.
- lstring.c grows the string table at two strings per slot, not one.
- ldump.c: strip level 2 drops only local variable names, keeping line info,
  source and upvalue names.

